Right</U></B>. Employee may revoke the delivery (and therefore the effectiveness) of this Release within the seven-day period beginning
on the date Employee executes this Release (such seven day period being referred to herein as the &ldquo;Release Revocation Period&rdquo;).
To be effective, such revocation must be in writing signed by Employee and must be received by [NAME] [ADDRESS] [E-MAIL] before 11:59
p.m., Bethesda, Maryland time, on the last day of the Release Revocation Period. If an effective revocation is delivered in the foregoing
manner and timeframe, no Termination Benefits shall be provided and this Release shall be null and void. Provided that Employee does
not revoke his signature on this Agreement during the Release Revocation Period, this Agreement shall become effective on the eighth
(8th) day after Employee executes the Agreement.</P>

